          "prompt": "I’m tired of waiting for people to change,\nbuilding them up just to watch them cave.\nI can feel in my bones what’s possible,\nbut you keep turning away.\n\nYou make it sound like it’s everyone’s fault,\nbut I’ve tuned that noise out for good.\nThere’s only so long you can mourn someone\nwho’s still in the room.\n\nAnd you say it’s fine\nAnd I say, it’s fine.\n\nYou fade into the silence,\nI’m guilty of compliance,\nguarding every motion,\ncraving that oxytocin.\nLike tears from my child’s eye\nbut I haven’t cried since.\n\nThere’s nothing left to do,\njust wait outside the bar,\nstaring at my phone,\nhoping it lights when I’m alone.\nAll those years now wasted\nso near and yet so far.\n\nYou keep saying the world’s unfair,\nlike the world ever promised it’d care.\nI’ve been holding the line for both of us,\nbut the rope burned through somewhere.\n\nMaybe you’ll die inside your quiet,\nand I’ll just keep sweeping the floor.\nFunny how grief becomes routine\nwhen love’s not work anymore.\n\nAnd you say it’s fine\nAnd I say, it’s fine.\n\nYou fade into the silence,\nI’m guilty of compliance,\nguarding every motion,\ncraving that oxytocin.\nLike tears from my child’s eye\nbut I haven’t cried since.\n\nThere’s nothing left to do,\njust wait outside the bar,\nstaring at my phone,\nhoping it lights when I’m alone.\nAll those years now wasted\nso near and yet so far.\n\nI think I already buried you\nsomewhere between guilt and grace.\nThis one’s just the last funeral\nI’ll hold in your name.\n\nYou fade into the silence,\nI’m guilty of compliance,\nguarding every motion,\ncraving that oxytocin.\nLike tears from my child’s eye\nbut I haven’t cried since.\n\nThere’s nothing left to do,\njust wait outside the bar,\nstaring at my phone,\nhoping it lights when I’m alone.\nAll those years now wasted\nso near and yet so far.\n\n---\n\nLyrics written by SED NO1",
