        "metadata": {
          "tags": "World fusion minimalism with off-beat percussion, kaba-style hand drums, rubbery bass pulses, and vocal percussion woven like an instrument; verse stays sparse and hypnotic, pre-chorus opens with stacked chant swells, chorus lands on a short spell-like refrain with group responses. Add sand-shaker ticks, frame-drum accents, and reversed breathy swells. Gunky-funky, dry and intimate mix with warm room bloom., world fusion, funky",
          "prompt": "[Verse 1]\nBy the Hill it rose\nGrey on grey on grey\nA body left to dust\nA shape that would not stay\nWe stood there stunned and still\nThe air went thin and cold\nThen the mist began to climb\nLike stories being told\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh ah\nIt leaned to the West\nOh ah\nThen it turned its face\n\n[Chorus]\nWest wind take it\nWest wind break it\nWest wind shake it\nGone gone gone\nWest wind take it\nWest wind break it\nWest wind shake it\nGone gone gone\n\n[Verse 2]\nIt wore a pale disguise\nA shroud of moving ash\nFor one breath it looked alive\nThen folded into hush\nThe wind came sharp and clean\nA cut across the bone\nThe figure lost its name\nAnd faded on its own\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh ah\nIt leaned to the West\nOh ah\nThen it turned to rest\n\n[Chorus]\nWest wind take it\nWest wind break it\nWest wind shake it\nGone gone gone\nWest wind take it\nWest wind break it\nWest wind shake it\nGone gone gone\n\n[Bridge]\nNo hand could keep it here\nNo vow could make it last\nJust breath against the sky\nAnd nothing held it fast\nAh ah\nA little sigh\nAh ah\nAnd the Hill went quiet\n\n[Chorus]\nWest wind take it\nWest wind break it\nWest wind shake it\nGone gone gone\nWest wind take it\nWest wind break it\nWest wind shake it\nGone gone gone",
